OL,3,CProgramme listings for THU 9 APR
OL,4,G1930FRadio 3 in Concert
OL,5,     GFrom Birmingham, the CBSO plays
OL,6,     GRachmaninov's Rhapsody on a theme
OL,7,     Gof Paganini with pianist Nelson
OL,8,     GGoerner, alongside music by
OL,9,     GHindemith and Bartok's Concerto
OL,10,     Gfor Orchestra.
OL,11,G2145FThe Essay: Healing Musicians
OL,12,     GKate Kennedy meets Ludwig Quandt,
OL,13,     Gprincipal cellist of the Berlin
OL,14,     GPhilharmonic, to discover how an
OL,15,     Gunexpected injury forced him to
OL,16,     Grethink his life and career.
OL,17,G2200FNight Tracks
OL,18,     GSara Mohr-Pietsch presents an
OL,19,     Gadventurous, immersive soundtrack
OL,20,     Gfor late-night listening, from
OL,21,     Gclassical to contemporary and
OL,22,     Geverything in between.
OL,23,Vppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
